    "body": "In `blocks_relay_conn_tests`, the check that a transaction submitted over RPC is not announced to a block-relay-only peer looks for its txid among the peer's invs. The peer is a `P2PTxInvStore`, which negotiates wtxidrelay, so an announcement would carry the wtxid. The MiniWallet transaction has a witness, so its txid and wtxid differ, and the check passes whether or not the node announces it.\n\nThis checks the wtxid instead. To see the difference, open that connection as `outbound-full-relay`: the old check still passes, the new one fails.\n\n#35920 also edits `blocks_relay_conn_tests`; the two do not conflict.\n\nFound while porting these tests to https://github.com/btclib-org/bitcoin-node-tests.\n",
